{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_rotation_cutover_gate_is_fabric_wide_not_per_peer_any_live_gate_mismatch", "label": "The Role-A cutover gate is fabric-wide but the action it gates is per-peer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-cutover-gate-is-fabric-wide-not-per-peer.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With two gateways any_live and all_live coincide; with three or more, one peer's handshake moves every peer's CIDRs onto a device the others have no session on. all_live is the wrong correction \u2014 one unreachable peer would hold the cutover hostage indefinitely, which is worse than a bounded per-peer stall. Deliberately not fixed: build the three-gateway harness, watch it fail, then fix it."}, {"id": "docs_research_rotation_cutover_gate_is_fabric_wide_not_per_peer_predicate_reuse_antipattern", "label": "Antipattern \u2014 a predicate written for one question reused for a neighbouring one", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-cutover-gate-is-fabric-wide-not-per-peer.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Held five times on this branch: base_tun vs the active tun, a directive-time key snapshot vs the current key, any_live vs this peer's liveness."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_research_rotation_cutover_gate_is_fabric_wide_not_per_peer_any_live_gate_mismatch", "target": "docs_research_rotation_cutover_gate_is_fabric_wide_not_per_peer_predicate_reuse_antipattern", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-cutover-gate-is-fabric-wide-not-per-peer.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_rotation_cutover_gate_is_fabric_wide_not_per_peer_any_live_gate_mismatch", "target": "docs_research_in_step_rotation_cutover_arbitration_cutover_